      "solution": "import sys\n\n\ndef calibrate(readings, costs):\n    size = len(readings)\n    best_cost = None\n    optimal_count = 0\n    for first in range(2):\n        for second in range(2):\n            total_cost = costs[0][first] + costs[1][second]\n            previous, current = first, second\n            for i in range(size - 2):\n                next_state = readings[i] - previous - current\n                if next_state not in (0, 1):\n                    break\n                total_cost += costs[i + 2][next_state]\n                previous, current = current, next_state\n            else:\n                if previous + current + first != readings[-2]:\n                    continue\n                if current + first + second != readings[-1]:\n                    continue\n                if best_cost is None or total_cost < best_cost:\n                    best_cost = total_cost\n                    optimal_count = 1\n                elif total_cost == best_cost:\n                    optimal_count += 1\n    return best_cost, optimal_count\n\n\ndef main():\n    lines = sys.stdin.buffer\n    size = int(lines.readline())\n    readings = []\n    costs = []\n    for _ in range(size):\n        reading, closed, opened = map(int, lines.readline().split())\n        readings.append(reading)\n        costs.append((closed, opened))\n    cost, count = calibrate(readings, costs)\n    print(\"IMPOSSIBLE\" if cost is None else f\"{cost} {count}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
      "statement": "A museum exhibit has a ring of [[n]] beacons numbered from {{0}} to [[n]] - {{1}}. Each beacon can be closed or open. A sensor at beacon [[i]] reports how many of the three beacons starting at [[i]] are open. The three beacons are [[i]], ([[i]] + {{1}}) modulo [[n]], and ([[i]] + {{2}}) modulo [[n]].\n\nThe cost of closing or opening each beacon is given separately. Every beacon must be assigned a state. The total cost is the sum of the costs of the assigned states. Find the minimum total cost that matches every sensor reading, and count how many assignments attain that cost. Assignments are distinct if they differ at any numbered beacon.\n\nIf the readings cannot all be matched, print IMPOSSIBLE.",
