    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">A museum exhibit has a ring of <var>n</var> beacons numbered from <const>0</const> to <var>n</var> - <const>1</const>. Each beacon can be closed or open. A sensor at beacon <var>i</var> reports how many of the three beacons starting at <var>i</var> are open. The three beacons are <var>i</var>, (<var>i</var> + <const>1</const>) modulo <var>n</var>, and (<var>i</var> + <const>2</const>) modulo <var>n</var>.<br><br>The cost of closing or opening each beacon is given separately. Every beacon must be assigned a state. The total cost is the sum of the costs of the assigned states. Find the minimum total cost that matches every sensor reading, and count how many assignments attain that cost. Assignments are distinct if they differ at any numbered beacon.<br><br>If the readings cannot all be matched, print IMPOSSIBLE.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> An integer <var>n</var>, the number of beacons.<br><strong>Next <var>n</var> lines:</strong> Three space-separated integers <var>reading</var>, <var>closedCost</var>, and <var>openCost</var> for each beacon, in order from beacon <const>0</const> to beacon <var>n</var> - <const>1</const>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>One line:</strong> Two space-separated integers, the minimum total cost and the number of assignments attaining that cost, or IMPOSSIBLE if no assignment matches every reading.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\"><const>3</const> &le; <var>n</var> &le; <const>200</const><br><const>0</const> &le; <var>reading</var> &le; <const>3</const><br><const>0</const> &le; <var>closedCost</var>, <var>openCost</var> &le; <const>1000000000</const><br>The total cost can exceed the range of a signed 32-bit integer.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">5\n2 5 0\n2 1 5\n2 2 5\n2 3 1\n1 2 9</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">9 1</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
